    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green. \n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I implemented so that new owners get a `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `customerCode` field mapped to a `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **API schema** (`resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n3. **Database schemas** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table in all four dialect schemas (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests, h2, mysql, postgres), since `ddl-auto=none`.\n\n4. **Create logic** (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`) \u2014 in `addOwner`, before saving, the code is assigned via a new `nextCustomerCode(lastName)` helper:\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (non-letters stripped for robustness),\n   - `NNNN` = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` (verifying `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and the global +1 sequence) and the full suite both pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
